; Fixture scene for the remote scene-tree debugger tests (RIDER-140036).
; Autoloaded, so it is a sibling of the main scene under /root and makes autoloads observable.
;
; Child counts are chosen against ChildFetchStrategy.BulkFetchThreshold:
;   Narrow  = 32  children -> at the threshold, per-child (slow) path
;   Wide    = 33  children -> one over the threshold, compiled-lambda (fast) path
;   Chunked = 150 children -> fast path AND one level of [a..b] chunking (ChunkSize = 100)
; Narrow and Wide hold the same names on purpose: the two paths must render identically.
;
; Awkward node names (unicode, spaces, dashes, leading digits, a surrogate pair) are held twice, on both sides of
; the same threshold:
;   SpecialNames     = 6  children -> names resolved one by one through the Name property
;   SpecialNamesWide = 33 children -> the same six names first, then fillers, so they arrive through the
;                                     length-prefixed ChildNamesManifest instead. The manifest counts UTF-16 units,
;                                     which is why one name is a surrogate pair.
;
; Declarative on purpose - no C# here, so the fixture cannot break the build.

[gd_scene format=3]

[node name="SceneTreeFixture" type="Node"]

[node name="Narrow" type="Node" parent="."]

[node name="Child00" type="Node" parent="Narrow"]

[node name="Child01" type="Node" parent="Narrow"]

